Files covered
-------------

    src/engine/render/assets/sprites/card/playing_card_assets_large.svg
    src/engine/render/assets/sprites/card/playing_card_assets_corner_pips.svg
    src/engine/render/assets/sprites/card/playing_card_assets_all_corner_pips.svg

        The vector source, in the three cuts this project offers as decks.
        All are modified; see "Modifications" below.

    src/engine/render/assets/sprites/atlas/classic/card_assets-0.png
    src/engine/render/assets/sprites/atlas/indexed/card_assets-0.png
    src/engine/render/assets/sprites/atlas/all-corner-pips/card_assets-0.png

        The texture atlas pages `yarn build:atlas` renders from the three
        sheets above, a directory per deck. These are checked in rather than
        built on demand, so the artwork is redistributed with this repository
        in raster form as well as in vector form, and these pages carry its
        license with them.

        Each deck's second page, `card_assets-1.png`, holds only the pile
        placeholders cut from `card_placeholders.svg`, which is this project's
        own work. It is named here because the split between the two pages is
        a packing detail that can change, not a promise: whichever page a card
        frame lands on is covered.

        The `card_assets_atlas.json` beside each page records frame names and
        coordinates rather than artwork, and is covered only insofar as it is
        part of the same derived work.

    Copies of those pages in any build output, which `yarn build` emits into
    `dist/assets/` under content-hashed names.

