Modifications
-------------

The vector source carries changes made by this project rather than by the
original author, which LGPL-3.0 requires be stated. Each file states its own
on its face, in a comment at the top.

Applying to all three files:

  * The cards were moved apart onto a regular grid with a gutter between them.
    As drawn, cards abutted and shared a single hairline rule along each
    boundary, which the atlas cutter had to locate by ink coverage and tell
    apart from the court cards' inner frames. Only the position of each card
    changed; the artwork within each card is untouched.

Applying to `playing_card_assets_corner_pips.svg` and
`playing_card_assets_all_corner_pips.svg`:

  * Suit pips were added in the blank margin at the top right — on the aces
    and courts in `corner_pips`, and on all 52 cards in `all_corner_pips`. A
    fanned tableau column leaves only the top 45 of a card's 307 design units
    showing, and the deck places its own corner suit pip below that line. The
    added pips repeat each card's corner index pip at its own size, in a layer
    of their own; they cover no artwork, and no original element was edited.

So `playing_card_assets_large.svg` is the artwork as its author drew it, laid
out differently, and the two pip decks are that same layout with a layer added.
All three are reproducible from the upstream file, which is in this
repository's history as the first committed revision of
`playing_card_assets_large.svg` — the only one of the three that ever existed
here unmodified, the other two having been added already carrying their
changes.

